## STEP 1 — DELTA

- [NEW] api.signageos.io: **Split auth gates fingerprinted by error code.** JWT-gated (`403105 WRONG_JWT_TOKEN`): `/v1/device`, `/v1/device/{uid}/{alive,telemetry/latest,screenshot,debug,telemetry/set}`, `/v1/account`, `/v1/emulator`, `/v1/license`, `/v1/company`, `/v1/location`, `/v1/content-guard/item`. Legacy org client-secret gated (`403083`→`403075 NO_ORGANIZATION`): `/v1/device/{uid}/{peer-recovery,brightness,resolution}` **and** `/v1/device` + `/v2/device` lists (accept legacy `X-Auth`). Account-token gated (`403074`→`403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT`): `/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token` (accepts `x-oauth-client_id`/`x-oauth-client_secret` or `X-Auth id:secret`).
- [NEW] SDK source RAG (cloned `github.com/signageos/sdk`): `requester.ts:18` — `X-Auth = accessToken(JWT) | clientId:secret`. `apiTools.ts:133` + `sosControlHelper.ts:119-137` — **org credentials are obtained by calling `GET /v1/organization/{uid}` with ACCOUNT auth and reading `oauthClientId`/`oauthClientSecret`** from the response (`Organization.ts createApiV1` reuses them as full API X-Auth). Confirms account→org credential retrieval is the designed flow.
- [NEW] box.signageos.io: `/status` hostname rotated again (`jrm7x`); CSP/18× ACAO unchanged — previously confirmed findings remain live (no new delta).

## STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE

- [PRIO] api.signageos.io `/v1/organization/{uid}` + `/security-token`: attack 8, business 10, tech 8, gate 6 (needs account token), cloud 5, fresh 8 → **7.7**
- [PRIO] api.signageos.io `/v1/device/{uid}/peer-recovery` (legacy client-secret gate): attack 8, business 9, tech 7, gate 5, cloud 5, fresh 7 → **7.1**
- [PRIO] api.signageos.io `/v2/device` (legacy-auth acceptance): attack 6, business 7, tech 7, gate 5, cloud 4, fresh 6 → **5.9**

## STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES

[HYP] Cross-tenant org OAuth client-secret disclosure via account token
class: IDOR
asset: api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid} (GET)
confidence: 65
reasoning: SDK fetches an org's oauthClientId/oauthClientSecret using only ACCOUNT auth (sosControlHelper.ts:130-136 → organizationManagement.get(uid) with accountDI; RestApi.ts:65). If server does not verify account∈company→org, any account token reads any org's full API credential.
evidence_needed: `GET /v1/organization/<foreign-uid>` with own account token returns 200 containing `oauthClientSecret`.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED: `GET /v1/organization/<own-org> -H "X-Auth: <ownId>:<ownToken>"` baseline 200; repeat with foreign org UID → 200 = cross-tenant credential disclosure; then use leaked secret as org X-Auth on `/v1/device`.
impact: obtain any tenant's org API credential → full device/content/timing/firmware control; CRITICAL
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Cross-tenant org-token minting via account credentials on security-token endpoint
class: IDOR
asset: api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token (GET/POST)
confidence: 60
reasoning: live gate is account-scoped (403074/403076, accepts x-oauth-client_id/secret or X-Auth id:secret), not JWT nor org-scoped; SDK builds `organization/<uid>/security-token` with the same account auth (OrganizationTokenManagement.ts:29-32). Cross-tenant iff path-UID is not bound to the authenticated account's company.
evidence_needed: with own account creds, `GET /v1/organization/<foreign-uid>/security-token` returns 200 (not 403).
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED: baseline `GET /v1/organization/<own>/security-token` = 200; foreign UID → 200 = cross-tenant; `POST {"name":"x"}` mints a working org token.
impact: mint org tokens for any tenant → full foreign-device control; CRITICAL
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Cross-tenant peer-recovery write via legacy org client-secret (device UID not bound to org)
class: IDOR
asset: api.signageos.io/v1/device/{uid}/peer-recovery (GET/PUT), /brightness, /resolution
confidence: 55
reasoning: only these device subresources are client-secret-gated (403083/403075) instead of JWT (403105); deviceUid is a client-supplied path arg; org is derived only from X-Auth credential, so org→device membership is the sole barrier.
evidence_needed: with own org X-Auth, `GET/PUT /v1/device/<foreign-uid>/peer-recovery` returns 200.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED: baseline `GET /v1/device/<own-uid>/peer-recovery` = 200; foreign UID → 200 = cross-tenant; `PUT {"enabled":true,"urlLauncherAddress":"https://attacker"}` confirms write.
impact: read/overwrite any tenant's device recovery launcher config → device+content takeover; HIGH→CRITICAL
testability: AUTH_HELPED

## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

- [PARKED] v2 API partial-migration authz drift: passive probes this run show only `/v2/device`+`/v2/firmware` exist, both 403 with gates identical to v1; all other /v2 paths 404; `/v2/device` accepts legacy X-Auth exactly like `/v1/device`. No drift observed; remaining proof requires AUTH_HELPED cross-version compare. confidence <40.
- [FINAL] 1) org client-secret disclosure via `GET /v1/organization/{uid}` (65)  2) org-token minting via `/security-token` (60)  3) peer-recovery cross-tenant write (55)

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

- [NEXT] HUMAN: Obtain any legitimate account token (e.g. `sos login` Auth0 device flow — audience `https://sos-production.us.auth0.com/api/v2/`, clientId `8AU8D3zJ4mK8gszZP3gZO0nv9DusSNjV` per `cli/src/Auth/predefinedRegions.ts`), then run the single sharpest test: `GET https://api.signageos.io/v1/organization/<own-org-uid> -H "X-Auth: <ownAccountId>:<ownAccountToken>"` (baseline, expect `oauthClientSecret`), then `GET /v1/organization/<foreign-org-uid>` — a 200 with secret proves cross-tenant credential disclosure. Passive surface is exhausted; this converts the SDK-proven account→org credential chain into a POC.

