- [LEARN] REJECTED AUTH @ api.signageos.io/v2/*: passive probes show /v2 is a 2-route selective port with gates identical to /v1 — no authz drift, no unauthenticated route.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED IDOR-path @ api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}: SDK source proves oauthClientSecret is returned to account-token holders; cross-tenant outcome hinges on server-side company check — highest-value AUTH_HELPED candidate.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ box.signageos.io/status + CORS: reconfirmed live this run (hostname rotating, 18 ACAO, no credentials).

## STEP 7 — RISK SCORE

- [RISK] box.signageos.io: 72 — unchanged: Auth0 OAuth2 dashboard, API-token minting origin, broad CSP trust boundary (40+ origins); /status + CORS confirmed live; exposure stable.
- [RISK] api.signageos.io: 80 — raised: 60+ endpoints confirmed with tri-modal auth (JWT / legacy client-secret / account-token), SDK proves org OAuth client-secret is retrievable with account auth, making any single account token a candidate cross-tenant pivot; /status leaks infra; risk concentrated on org-boundary authorization.
