## STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] api.signageos.io/openapi.yml — public OpenAPI 3.0 spec (v50.4.0, 1.57MB, HTTP 200 unauth) on the in-scope host: 286 paths / 430 ops (219 GET, 97 PUT, 72 POST, 42 DELETE), full per-endpoint security model. Replaces the bundle.js-derived map as the authoritative catalog.
- [CHANGED] REST-API docs migrated off Zendesk: old article IDs (4405231278482, 4405239033234) now 404; live at docs.signageos.io/api/ (Docusaurus), which itself links the in-scope openapi.yml.
- [NEW] Spec-confirmed: `GET /v1/organization/{organizationUid}` is **both-scheme** (XAuthOrganization + XAuthAccount) and its 200 schema includes `oauthClientId` + `oauthClientSecret` → account-token read of org OAuth credentials is a documented valid request shape.
- [NEW] Spec-confirmed: `GET/POST /v1/organization/{organizationUID}/security-token` are **XAuthAccount-only** (56 account-only ops total, incl. /v1/company/*, /v1/organization, /v1/system-log, /v1/bulk-provisioning/recipe/{recipeUid}, /v1/emulator).
- [NEW] Spec-confirmed: `POST /v1/account/security-token` takes `identification`/`password` as **query params** (credential-in-query MISCONFIG candidate).
- [NEW] Spec-confirmed: **0 of 430 ops** lack both security schemes → no unauthenticated API surface exists by design.
- [NEW] Spec-confirmed: v2 = only `/v2/device` + `/v2/firmware` (narrows the v2 authz-drift hypothesis to two routes).
- [CHANGED] Live re-probe (2026-08-07 22:0x): `/v1/company`, `/v1/system-log`, `/v1/organization/{uid}/member` → 403 WRONG_JWT (403105); `/v1/bulk-provisioning/recipe/{uid}` → 403 MISSING_CLIENT_SECRET (403083); api & box `/status` still 200 (box pod still gkzcp).

