## STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] sdk/requester.ts + cli/helper.ts: `X-Auth` is `<clientId>:<secret>` (legacy) or raw `<accessToken>` (JWT). Legacy auth NEVER sends `organizationUid` query (sending it yields INVALID_QUERY_PARAMS) → for legacy creds the org context is **derived entirely from the credential**, so the org→resource membership check is the sole cross-tenant barrier.
- [NEW] cli/organizationFacade.ts `getOrganization(uid)`: first-party code calls `GET /v1/organization/{uid}` with **account-level auth** (JWT or `identification:apiSecurityToken`) and returns the body verbatim, which includes `oauthClientId`+`oauthClientSecret`; the uid is an arbitrary client-supplied `--organization-uid` flag → first-party confirmation of H1's exact endpoint/response.
- [NEW] sdk/OrganizationTokenManagement: exact routes confirmed — `GET`/`POST /v1/organization/{organizationUid}/security-token` (POST body `{"name":...}`), `DELETE .../security-token/{tokenId}` → H2 recipe locked.
- [NEW] sdk/DevicePeerRecoveryManagement: `GET`/`PUT /v1/device/{deviceUid}/peer-recovery` (PUT body incl `urlLauncherAddress`) → H3 recipe locked.
- [NEW] cli `.env.production`: public Auth0 clientId `8AU8D3zJ4mK8gszZP3gZO0nv9DusSNjV` + audience `https://sos-production.us.auth0.com/api/v2/` + device-code flow → JWT persisted to `~/.sosrc`; public client ID only, no secret. Box/CLI auth model fully mapped.
- [NEW] Passive `/v2/*` probe: only `/v2/device` exists (403 JWT-gated, `403105 WRONG_JWT_TOKEN`); `/v2/license|alert|location|content|organization|account` all 404 → v2 is a selective device-only port, no pre-auth bypass surface.

